						<initial/>
						<documentation value="Bituminous tar or asphalt and/or oil or bitumen bound, mix-in-place surfaces (often referred to as &quot;earth cement&quot;). &#xA;[note: A bituminous tar or asphalt surface is prepared by digging up the surface, mixing the material with bitumen or oil binder, and surfacing the surface with the resulting mixture. Bitumen is the family name for tar which is derived from coal, or asphalt which is derived from oil. .]"/>
